PULP BENCHMARK SUITE LICENSE NOTICE

Repository-authored scripts, Bender manifests, testbench and simulation support
code, and documentation are licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0;
see LICENSE.Apache-2.0, unless another license is explicitly identified.

The generated benchmark packages aggregate independently developed components.
The RTL-only package contains hardware designs and supporting source code.
The simulation package additionally contains testbenches, simulation support
code, compiled firmware, and simulation data. No single license applies to
either package as a whole. Release archives identify their contents as rtl or
simulation in PACKAGE_KIND.

Each source tree remains subject to its original license terms. The applicable
license and notice files are preserved alongside the corresponding sources in
each design's main/ and dependencies/ directories. In the simulation package,
licenses and notices for simulation support, firmware, and data are also
included under each design's data/ and variants/<variant>/data/ directories.
Associated README files describe provenance and toolchain versions. Individual
source files may also carry SPDX license identifiers or copyright notices;
those identifiers and notices govern those files.

Third-party testbench code, firmware, runtime libraries, and simulation data
remain subject to their respective licenses and notices. Their inclusion does
not place them under the license for repository-authored code. Redistribution
of each component remains subject to its applicable license and notice
requirements.

Benchmark wrapper files carrying the SPDX identifier Apache-2.0 are licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0; see LICENSE.Apache-2.0. Support files
carrying SHL-0.51 are licensed under the Solderpad Hardware License, Version
0.51; see LICENSE.SHL-0.51.

Nothing in either package changes, replaces, or broadens the license granted by
any upstream project or contributor.
